From 46326dff175ea4f1596f7221a0e3de46053de17a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kayori <thatzokay@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:34:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] grate: expose Z24S8 and Z24X8 depth buffers as Z16NL plus an
 S8 stencil plane

The Tegra 3 has no 24-bit depth. The Windows RT driver (nvd3dum.dll, found by
static analysis) implements D24S8/D24X8 as 16-bit non-linear depth (surface
format Z16NL, slot 0) and, for stencil, a separate S8 surface in slot 2 that
follows the depth plane in the same buffer. Do the same, so EGL clients that
ask for a 24-bit depth / 8-bit stencil config (glutin: Catacomb's Epitaph,
Tabula, Tzompantli) get one without per-application patches.

* Z24X8, X8Z24, Z24_UNORM_S8_UINT and S8_UINT_Z24_UNORM select Z16NL. The depth
  plane is 2 bytes per pixel, 256-byte aligned rows; a stencil format adds an
  S8 plane (1 byte per pixel, 256-byte aligned rows) after it. Not samplable.
* The framebuffer binds the stencil plane as surface 2 (reloc offset past the
  depth plane). With more than one colour buffer (colour output i is surface
  i + 1, so output 1 would collide) stencil is dropped with a message.
* Stencil state: QR_S_TEST_FRONT/BACK, QR_S_CTRL and GLOBAL_S_OPERATION_FRONT/BACK
  are emitted on every draw, one-sided stencil using the front state for both
  faces; the stencil reference comes from set_stencil_ref(). The ops use the
  Windows driver's order (zero, keep, replace, incr-sat, decr-sat, invert,
  incr-wrap, decr-wrap). DW Z_TEST is enabled when depth or stencil is.
* Clears fill the planes separately: the depth plane with the Z16NL code (the
  inverse of the driver's decode table), the stencil plane with a byte.
* Removes the GRATE_Z24_CODE experiment hook.

Builds for armv7. NOT tested on the tablet yet.
